# Keep line-ending normalization away from SHA-locked binary assets.
#
# Netpbm P2/P5 files are plain pixel dumps, not line-oriented text. Git's
# text heuristic can still classify them as text, so a Windows checkout with
# core.autocrlf=true rewrites every LF as CRLF and silently breaks the
# recorded SHA-256 in the matching query packet.
*.pgm -text
*.ppm -text
*.pbm -text
*.pnm -text
